  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: arbitrary code execution via the ImageMath.eval\n     environment parameter (ELSCVE-187962)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2023-50447.patch: reject environment keys that\n       contain \"__\" or shadow a builtin before they are merged into the\n       execution namespace in src/PIL/ImageMath.py, so an injected name can\n       no longer satisfy the expression allowlist. Adds a regression test in\n       Tests/test_imagemath.py.\n     - CVE-2023-50447\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: denial of service via unbounded allocation when\n     measuring or rendering very long strings\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2023-44271.patch: add ImageFont.MAX_STRING_LENGTH\n       and check it at each text entry point in src/PIL/ImageFont.py before\n       the C layer allocates. Adds a regression test in\n       Tests/test_imagefont.py.\n     - CVE-2023-44271",
